# scratch: proof runs materialise a ref here, so this tree holds WHOLE COPIES of test files (measured
# 2026-10-09: 879 *.test.ts under four .scratch dirs). Two things went wrong while it was unignored: a
# `git add -A` swept an in-flight doc edit into an unrelated commit (amendment 196's record landed inside an
# M5 commit and described a tree that did not exist), and a root-level vitest run would have graded those
# stale copies. `vitest.config.ts` excludes them; this keeps them out of commits too.
.scratch/

# vitest's config loader writes a TIMESTAMPED bundle next to the config it compiles
# (`apps/studio/vitest.config.ts.timestamp-<ms>-<hash>.mjs`) and does not remove it. Measured 2026-10-20:
# one such file sat untracked in the studio package — a `git add -A` away from a commit that carries a
# build artefact. It is regenerated on every run, so ignoring the pattern is the durable fix; the file
# itself could not be removed by the agent (the local launcher for recoverable deletion is unavailable).
vitest.config.ts.timestamp-*.mjs

# another tool's own memory directory, which holds no part of this project's build. Ignored for the same
# reason .scratch/ is: an untracked foreign tree in the working directory is one `git add -A` away from being
# swept into an unrelated commit, and amendment 215 records that happening once already.
.workbuddy-ai/

# scratch scripts and commit-message drafts. Measured 2026-10-25: 361 untracked `tmp_*.py` debug
# scripts and a `commit_msg.txt` in the working tree — the same hazard `.scratch/` and
# `.workbuddy-ai/` above exist for, one `git add -A` away from being swept into an unrelated
# commit (amendments 196 and 215 each record that happening). None is tracked
# (`git ls-files "tmp_*"` → 0), so ignoring the pattern deletes nothing; `git add -f` still
# forces one in if a scratch file is ever meant to land.
tmp_*
commit_msg.txt
